description:
FILED s516b (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-12) from member 3's Type::Tiny load probe (#3240 fixed: Type::Tiny.pm now LOADS; Types::Standard is the next stop).

TYPE::TINY: `use Types::Standard -all` dies "Parent must be an instance of Type::Tiny".  Type/Tiny.pm:1458 overrides isa and ends `$self->SUPER::isa( @_ )`; Type::Tiny has no @ISA, so SUPER:: finishes at UNIVERSAL::isa -- and the `@_` reaches it UNFLATTENED, so every `$type->isa('Type::Tiny')` is false.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs main code f9455ea9):

    package Foo;
    sub new { bless {}, shift }
    sub i1 { my $self = shift; $self->SUPER::isa('Foo') ? 1 : 0 }
    sub i2 { my $self = shift; $self->SUPER::isa(@_) ? 1 : 0 }
    sub i3 { my $self = shift; my @a = @_; $self->SUPER::isa(@a) ? 1 : 0 }
    sub i4 { my ($self, $c) = @_; $self->SUPER::isa($c) ? 1 : 0 }
    sub i5 { my $self = shift; UNIVERSAL::isa($self, @_) ? 1 : 0 }
    package main;
    my $f = Foo->new;
    print join(' ', $f->i1, $f->i2('Foo'), $f->i3('Foo'), $f->i4('Foo'), $f->i5('Foo')), "\n";

perl `1 1 1 1 1`; PCL `1 0 0 1 0`.  And `my @two = ($f, 'Foo'); UNIVERSAL::isa(@two)` dies in PCL with a raw CL "invalid number of arguments: 1" (perl: 1).  The plain METHOD spelling `$f->isa(@a)` / `$f->can(@m)` / `$f->DOES(@a)` is right (the dispatch flattens).

CAUSE: the emission passes an array argument as the raw vector (`(UNIVERSAL::pl-isa $self @_)`, `(p-super-call $self "isa" "main" @_)`) -- the calling convention: a CALLEE flattens (p-args-body / p-flatten-args).  The UNIVERSAL entry points (UNIVERSAL::pl-isa / pl-can / pl-DOES, fixed-arity CL lambda lists) and %pcl-super-fallback's built-in arms (`(apply #'%p-isa-mro obj args)`) are callees that never flatten.  FIX at the runtime (cl/pcl-runtime.lisp): those entries take &rest and flatten through the ONE value flattener (%p-flatten-arg-values) before reading obj/class.

=== DONE (s516b, filler 2) ===
cl/pcl-runtime.lisp: UNIVERSAL::isa / can / DOES take their arguments as a LIST and flatten it (%p-builtin-arg-list = %p-flatten-arg-values when an array or hash is among them), and die perl's `Usage: UNIVERSAL::isa(reference, kind)` / `UNIVERSAL::can(object-ref, method)` / `invocant->DOES(kind)` on fewer than two; %pcl-super-fallback's built-in arms read the same flattened list.  The reproducer prints `1 1 1 1 1` = perl; `UNIVERSAL::isa(@two)` = 1 (was a CL arity error).  Guard Pl/t/universal-01.t 7 -> 8 rows (perl oracle), inverse-verified on main.  Type::Tiny: `$type->isa('Type::Tiny')` is true now; Types::Standard's next stop is #3281 (core B).
